+# LeJeune Bolt Company: social, clients, and projects
+
+Research date: 2026-08-25.
+
+Packet context (not independently verified on the public web): `explorations/lejeune-bolt-agentic-demo/CAPTURE.md` records a 2026-08-25 conversation with Jackson LeJeune, an employee in sales / marketing / logistics and son of an executive. The lunch pitch next week is framed around veterans retiring, Microsoft 365 as the system of record, and a demo that ingests office data into a fastener knowledge graph. This file is the public-web half of that brief. Packet-only claims are marked **PACKET / UNVERIFIED**.
+
+Do not confuse **LeJeune Bolt Company** (Burnsville fastener distributor, this subject) with **LeJeune Steel Company** (Minneapolis structural fabricator, APi Group, separate firm that split off in 1977). Both appear on Twin Cities steel jobs. Mixing them invents a customer relationship that the public record does not support.
+
+---
+
+## Company profile
+
+LeJeune Bolt Company is a privately held Minnesota structural fastener distributor. Public self-description: supplier of structural bolts, installation tools, concrete anchors, stud welding, and general-line fasteners, and exclusive source of the patented TNA (Torque + Angle) fastening system using ASTM F3148 144 ksi fixed-spline assemblies. Tagline on the homepage: "Big Bolts. Big Projects. Big, Big Service." ([lejeunebolt.com](https://lejeunebolt.com/))
+
+**Legal / SAM.** SAM.gov lists legal name LEJEUNE BOLT CO, Burnsville MN, Unique Entity ID W3HMKMJB7DA7, CAGE 1LMB9, incorporated in Minnesota, entity structure corporate (not tax exempt), business types for-profit and Subchapter S corporation, also self-certified small disadvantaged business. Registered 2002-04-02. Business start date 1977-01-03. Officers named: Karla Berg (Controller), Jeff Greene (President), Chad Larson (title blank on the aggregator page). Snapshot accessed 2026-08-25 listed status Expired, with activation 2025-08-29 and expiration 2026-08-27. Treat SAM status as time-sensitive. ([opengovus.com/sam-entity/W3HMKMJB7DA7](https://opengovus.com/sam-entity/W3HMKMJB7DA7))
+
+**Locations.** Headquarters: 3500 West Highway 13, Burnsville, MN 55337. Western Region: 3655 Placentia Ct, Chino, CA 91710. Main 952.890.7700, toll-free 800.USA.BOLT (872.2658), Western 909.529.7577 / 877.684.4091. Hours stated as 8:00 am to 5:00 pm CT (MN) and PST (CA), weekdays. ([lejeunebolt.com](https://lejeunebolt.com/); [shortspansteelbridges.org supplier page](https://www.shortspansteelbridges.org/suppliers/lejeune-bolt-company/))
+
+**Founding.** The live homepage says the firm began in a small warehouse in Burnsville in 1976. The 2016 brochure says a small garage in Minneapolis in 1977. LinkedIn and SAM use 1977. YouTube and the 2026 NASCC exhibitor copy celebrate a 50th anniversary in 2026. AISC's 2021 obituary of Laurence "Larry" LeJeune (LeJeune Steel) resolves the family split: in 1967 Larry and his brother Tom bought LeJeune Steel from their father; in 1977 Larry bought Tom out, "who in turn developed a structural fastener company, LeJeune Bolt." ([lejeunebolt.com](https://lejeunebolt.com/); [brochure PDF](https://lejeunebolt.com/lbc/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/lejeunebrochure.pdf); [AISC, 2021-09-09](https://www.aisc.org/modern-steel/news/laurence-larry-lejeune-former-aisc-board-member-dies-at-85/); [YouTube @LeJeuneBolt](https://www.youtube.com/@LeJeuneBolt); [Modern Steel Construction, April 2026 exhibitor highlights](https://lsc-pagepro.mydigitalpublication.com/article/2026+Exhibitor+Highlights/5120884/861568/article.html))
+
+**West Coast.** A 2021 capability statement says LeJeune added a West Coast field office and warehouse in 2013. The Boeing 777X wing-factory portfolio page calls that job one of the first large-scale projects out of Chino. ([capability statement PDF](https://lejeunebolt.com/lbc/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/03-158-Capability-Statement.pdf); [Boeing 777X page](https://lejeunebolt.com/portfolio-items/boeing-777x-wing-factory/))
+
+**Size.** LinkedIn: privately held, 11-50 employees, 14 employees discoverable on the public company page, ~790 followers on 2026-08-25. The 2021 capability statement claims "over 70,000 square feet of warehouse space" and next-day / two-day service to most of the U.S. Short Span Steel Bridges copy: "average industry tenure of over 20 years." Aggregator headcounts (16, 20) and revenue figures ($4.4M Datanyze; $10M one directory; $10-24.9M Thomasnet) are **UNVERIFIED**. USDOT 3475398 lists one owned straight truck, private property, building materials / construction cargo, intrastate non-HM (MCS-150 dated 2020-08-24). ([LinkedIn company](https://www.linkedin.com/company/lejeune-bolt-company); [capability statement](https://lejeunebolt.com/lbc/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/03-158-Capability-Statement.pdf); [dot.report/usdot/3475398](https://dot.report/usdot/3475398))
+
+**Sites.** Primary: [lejeunebolt.com](https://lejeunebolt.com/). TNA product site: [tightenright.com](https://www.tightenright.com/). Tool rentals: [rentals.lejeunebolt.com](https://rentals.lejeunebolt.com/). WooCommerce shop for tool sales. WordPress 7.1 / WooCommerce 11.0.1 on the homepage scrape. Sales inbox published as sales@lejeunebolt.com.
+
+**Markets named on the site.** Bridges, commercial, government and municipal, industrial. Capability statement primary work area: U.S., Canada, South America, Mexico, Europe.
