+## How the fastener distribution trade talks (X and LinkedIn)
+
+LeJeune itself talks on LinkedIn and almost not on X. The surrounding trade's X vocabulary, from searches on 2026-08-25:
+
+**Hashtags in actual posts.** `#FastenerNews` `#Fasteners` `#fastenerdistributor` `#fastenerdistributors` `#distribution` `#manufacturing` `#supplychain` `#FDI` `#industrialfasteners` `#fastenerindustry` `#FastenerStandards` `#FastenerTraining` `#NASCC` `#NASCC26` `#AISC` `#Bolting` `#StructuralBolting` `#SteelErection` `#SteelConstruction` `#WorldStandardsDay`. LeJeune/Larson also use `#SteelErection` and `#StructuralEngineering` on the NASCC 2026 post.
+
+**Communities and recurring objects.**
+
+- **Fastener Distributor Index (FDI)** and Forward-Looking Indicator, published via FCH Sourcing Network / @SourceFasteners, amplified by [@FastenerNews](https://x.com/FastenerNews). Example: 2025-02-10, FDI 47.6, FLI 49.9, 56 views, hashtags include `#fastenerdistributor` ([status/1888951883760332988](https://x.com/FastenerNews/status/1888951883760332988)). 2024-10-16 FDI 59.0 ([status/1846584241452155119](https://x.com/FastenerNews/status/1846584241452155119)).
+- **NFDA** (National Fastener Distributors Association): Executive Summit, member webinars. [@LindstromQuali1](https://x.com/LindstromQuali1) 2026-08-13 attending 2026 NFDA Executive Summit (1 like, 27 views). [@FastenerSchool](https://x.com/FastenerSchool) 2026-07-31 "LIVE Webinar for NFDA Members" (1 like, 84 views).
+- **IFI** (@IFIConnects): manufacturer-side, awards, standards. Congratulated Larson in 2021.
+- **Fully Threaded Radio** / Fastener Technology International: distributor interviews (Star Stainless, Würth).
+- **Regional fastener associations** named by other distributors, not by LeJeune: PAC-WEST, SWFA, MFDA, MWFA, SEFA, MAFDA, NEFDA, NFDA ([@EurolinkFSS](https://x.com/EurolinkFSS), 2026-05-27).
+- **NASCC / AISC** is where *structural* bolting actually lives. LeJeune's LinkedIn is written for fabricators and erectors, not for NFDA counter sales. xPM Solution 2026-04-14: GCs misunderstanding steel-contractor scope, tagged `#SteelConstruction` `#GeneralContractor` `#NASCC` ([status/2043852005571989568](https://x.com/SolutionXp65306/status/2043852005571989568)).
+- **Price/quote culture.** 2026-08-25 reply from a self-described wholesale fastener distributor: RFQs stuffed with McMaster part numbers, "I usually beat their price by at least half" ([status/2092316224156016817](https://x.com/JasonOdinMarsha/status/2092316224156016817), 32 views).
+
+**Implication for the demo.** Distributor Twitter is NFDA / FDI / import-tariff / McMaster-vs-wholesale. LeJeune's public voice is AISC / RCSC / AREMA / NASCC / F3148. A demo that only speaks "fastener distributor" will miss how they actually sell (specify TNA into the steel spec, train erectors, mill certs, sequence packs). A demo that only speaks "knowledge graph of ASTM" will miss the RFQ-and-availability grind in Jackson's day (`CAPTURE.md`).
